   Register reg = Register::FromCode(regCode);
diff a/js/src/jit/ppc64/MacroAssembler-ppc64.h b/js/src/jit/ppc64/MacroAssembler-ppc64.h
--- a/js/src/jit/ppc64/MacroAssembler-ppc64.h	2026-10-04 15:52:16.505454996 -0700
+++ b/js/src/jit/ppc64/MacroAssembler-ppc64.h	2026-10-04 15:58:55.520000000 -0700
@@ -32,12 +32,13 @@
 //
 // kNoPoolLoad64StanzaInsns (8): emitLoad64Stanza body — 8 NOPs that
 //   WriteLoad64Instructions later overwrites in place. Two shapes share
-//   the same 8-slot footprint with the .quad fixed at slots [6..7]:
-//     - POWER9+ (HasPOWER9()): addpcis + ld + b + 3 NOPs (2 dynamic insns,
-//       no LR clobber). Preferred path.
-//     - POWER8 fallback: mflr/bcl/mflr/mtlr/ld/b LR-bouncing sequence
-//       (6 dynamic insns, RAS-thrashing — kept only because P8 has no
-//       addpcis).
+//   the same 8-slot footprint:
+//     - POWER9+ (HasPOWER9()): addpcis + ld + b + 3 NOPs + .quad at
+//       slots [6..7] (2 dynamic insns, no LR clobber).
+//     - POWER8: lis/ori/sldi/oris/ori patchable immediate + 3 NOPs (no
+//       LR/r0 clobber, no data in the I-stream). Updating the value
+//       rewrites instructions, so live-code patchers must flush the
+//       I-cache over all 8 slots.
 //
 // kNoPoolPatchableBranchInsns (10): patchable far call / jump /
 //   unconditional branch. Three alternative shapes, all fitting the
